Given, equation of lines are

\begin{aligned}
\frac{x+3}{3} & =\frac{y-1}{5}=\frac{z+3}{4} \\
\text { and } \quad \frac{x+1}{1} & =\frac{y-4}{4}=\frac{z-5}{2}
\end{aligned}

Direction ratios of line (i) : $ \lt  3,5,4\gt $
Direction ratios of line (ii) : $ \lt  1,4,2\gt $
We know angle between pair of lines is given by

\cos \theta=\left|\frac{a_1 a_2+b_1 b_2+c_1 c_2}{\sqrt{a_1^2+b_1^2+c_1^2} \sqrt{a_2^2+b_2^2+c_2^2}}\right|

where, $ \lt  a_1, b_1, c_1\gt $ and $ \lt  a_2, b_2, c_2\gt $ are direction ratios of respectively lines.

\begin{aligned}
& \cos \theta=\left|\frac{3 \times 1+5 \times 4+4 \times 2}{\sqrt{3^2+5^2+4^4} \sqrt{1^2+4^2+2^2}}\right| \\
& \quad=\left|\frac{3+20+8}{\sqrt{9+25+16} \sqrt{1+16+4}}\right|=\left|\frac{31}{5 \sqrt{2} \sqrt{21}}\right|=\frac{31}{5 \sqrt{42}} \\
& \theta=\cos ^{-1}\left(\frac{31}{5 \sqrt{42}}\right)
\end{aligned}

(D)<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\hat{n}=\left(\frac{\vec{a} \times \vec{b}}{|\vec{a} \times \vec{b}|}\right) \\
\vec{a} \times \vec{b}=\left|\begin{array}{rrr}
\hat{i} & \hat{j} & \hat{k} \\
1 & 2 & 1 \\
-2 & 1 & 3
\end{array}\right|=5 \hat{i}-5 \hat{j}+5 \hat{k} \\
|\vec{a} \times \vec{b}|=5 \sqrt{3} \\
\therefore \hat{n}=\frac{\hat{i}-\hat{j}+\hat{k}}{\sqrt{3}} \\
\text { or } \hat{n}=\frac{-\hat{i}+\hat{j}-\hat{k}}{\sqrt{3}}
\end{array}
\]

